---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro';
import { personSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { COMPANION_NAME, COMPANION_URL, CONSULTING_PRACTICE_NAME, SITE_URL } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About the Corrections Pest Reference. Maintained by Trenton S. Frazer, Board Certified Entomologist (BCE #B3413). Independent reference work anchored in primary-source regulatory documentation for jails, prisons, and detention facilities."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'About', url: `${SITE_URL}/about/` }]}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <JsonLd data={personSchema()} />
  </Fragment>

  <h1>About the Corrections Pest Reference</h1>

  <h2>What This Reference Is</h2>

  <p>
    The Corrections Pest Reference is a national reference work mapping U.S. federal,
    state, and agency pest control requirements for county jails, state prisons, federal
    prisons, and immigration detention facilities. Every requirement on this site is
    anchored to a primary source: the regulation itself, the agency's published standard,
    or a court's published opinion.
  </p>

  <p>
    Pest control in a correctional facility sits under several regimes at once: workplace
    sanitation rules for the staff, food codes for the kitchen, detention and prison
    standards for the people held there, pesticide licensing for whoever applies the
    product, and the constitutional standard courts apply to conditions of confinement.
    This reference puts the text of each in one place, with its source.
  </p>

  <p>
    Where verbatim text is publicly available, it is reproduced. Where a standard is
    licensed or paywalled, it is recorded by identifier and the limitation is disclosed.
    Where a commonly-circulated claim has been investigated and disconfirmed, the
    disconfirmation is published.
  </p>

  <p>
    It is a companion to the <a href={COMPANION_URL}>{COMPANION_NAME}</a>, which does
    the same work for hospitals and long-term care facilities, and follows the same
    methodology.
  </p>

  <h2>What This Reference Is Not</h2>

  <p>
    This reference is not legal advice. It is not a substitute for counsel, for a
    facility's own policies, or for qualified pest management professionals. It is not
    a marketing piece for any commercial pest control service. Citations should be
    verified against the primary source for any litigation-grade application.
  </p>

  <h2>Operator and Credentialing</h2>

  <p>
    The reference is maintained by Trenton S. Frazer, Board Certified Entomologist
    (BCE #B3413, General Entomology specialty), certified April 28, 2025 by the
    Entomological Society of America Certification Corporation. Mr. Frazer holds an
    M.S. in Entomology from the University of Florida and a B.A. from Brigham Young
    University. He has twenty years of operational experience in pest management field
    operations and quality assurance, most recently as Senior Director of Quality
    Assurance at Aptive Environmental, where he oversaw quality programs serving more
    than 640,000 customers across more than 80 operations centers.
  </p>

  <p>
    Credentials can be verified at
    <a href="https://entocert.org/roster" target="_blank" rel="noopener">entocert.org/roster</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclosure</h2>

  <p>
    Mr. Frazer is the founder of Falcon Pest Control (Mountain Supply LLC dba), a Utah
    licensed pest management operator serving government facilities, schools, multifamily
    housing, and other commercial and residential clients. Falcon employs licensed
    technicians whom he directs.
  </p>

  <p>
    He also maintains {CONSULTING_PRACTICE_NAME}, a national consulting practice through
    which his Board Certified Entomologist consulting, program review, Entomologist of
    Record engagements, and expert witness work are delivered. The BCE credential is held
    by Mr. Frazer personally; the practice is the vehicle through which he is retained.
  </p>

  <p>
    This reference is published independently of those operations. It does not market
    commercial services, and engagement with either operation is not required to use it.
    Facilities seeking commercial pest management or consulting services are welcome to
    evaluate any qualified provider; this reference does not endorse or recommend any
    specific vendor.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about the reference, corrections to published content, and suggestions
    for additional authorities may be directed to the operator through the contact route
    on the <a href="/consulting/">consulting page</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
